Intentionally empty.

cape-qemu.deb ships bios.bin / bios-256k.bin / vgabios*.bin built from
QEMU's bundled SeaBIOS (under qemu/roms/seabios/). qemu-build/build.sh
applies anti-VM-detection patches to the bundled SeaBIOS source before
`make bios` + `make vgabios` runs, so the bios files inside cape-qemu
are already patched.

A separate seabios-build workflow would let us bump SeaBIOS independently
of QEMU (~5 min compile vs ~25 min for QEMU). Day 1 doesn't need that —
the qemu-bundled SeaBIOS satisfies CAPE's analysis VM needs.

When to revisit:

- SeaBIOS version newer than QEMU bundles is needed.
- SeaBIOS-only patches need rolling without rebuilding QEMU.
- Operators want to roll back SeaBIOS independent of QEMU.

The live-installer's `qemu-build/kvm-qemu.sh install_seabios()` is the
reference for that path. apt-publish.yml's fan-in already has a slot for
seabios-build artifacts (cape-seabios-debs-*) that becomes active once
this workflow lands.
